    <node id="Bicycle">
      <data key="d0">Bicycle</data>
      <data key="d1">vehicle</data>
      <data key="d2">"A two-wheeled vehicle powered by pedaling."&lt;SEP&gt;A bicycle is a two-wheeled vehicle designed for riding, often used for transportation or exercise. In this particular case, the bicycle is characterized by its vibrant red color and black details, which include the tires and seat. It features a black frame with red accents, making it visually appealing. Additionally, the bicycle is depicted as leaning against a wall in the left section of the image, illustrating its functionality and suitability for both transportation and recreation.</data>
      <data key="d3">"Can be ridden for transportation;"pedal;"ride;"ride";"transport;"transportation";can be stored when not in use.";commute;exercise";recreation";ride";transport</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"Back section of the image, against the wall, indicating it is possibly stationary."'&lt;SEP&gt;The descriptions indicate that the bicycle is positioned against the wall in the background, parallel to the window and the back wall. Specifically, its handlebars are oriented away from the observer, suggesting a clear and unobstructed view of the bicycle's frame from the front. The emphasis on its placement against the wall reinforces the idea that the bicycle is a notable element within the space, yet situated in a way that does not dominate the visual field.</data>
      <data key="d7">The Bicycle is a two-wheeled vehicle distinguished by its striking red color and a traditional frame design, complemented by a black frame with red accents. It serves as a versatile mode of transportation and is commonly utilized for both leisure activities and fitness purposes. Positioned upright against a wall and also placed parallel to a window, the Bicycle is readily accessible, allowing for convenient use while simultaneously enhancing the room's decor. This dual functionality highlights the Bicycle's role not only as a practical means of transport but also as an appealing element of the domestic environment, embodying both practicality and aesthetic charm.</data>
