      <data key="d10">1772788752</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pliers">
      <data key="d0">Pliers</data>
      <data key="d1">tool</data>
      <data key="d2">"Hand tool with black rubber grips and metallic jaws"&lt;SEP&gt;Pliers are a hand tool characterized by black handles, either made of rubber or plastic, which provide a comfortable grip. The metallic components of the tool include its jaws, which are designed for various functions such as gripping, bending, and cutting. This versatile handheld tool is commonly used in various tasks that require precision and strength.&lt;SEP&gt;"Handheld tool with jaws used for gripping, bending, and cutting."</data>
      <data key="d3">"Grip;"grip;"gripping;bend;bend";bending";cut;cut";twisting</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">The pliers are located in the left region of the countertop, positioned diagonally and pointing away from the viewer. They are resting flat on the surface of the workspace, near the left edge of the kitchen counter.</data>
      <data key="d7">Left side of the kitchen counter, positioned diagonally.&lt;SEP&gt;Pliers are a versatile hand tool primarily used for gripping, bending, and cutting materials. In the workspace, a pair of pliers can be found lying flat on the surface, specifically positioned near the left edge of the countertop. This particular pair of pliers features black and red accents, enhancing its appearance while serving practical functions. They are designed to grip and manipulate various objects, making them essential for a variety of tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pliers are a pair lying flat on the countertop, equipped with black and red accents, suitable for various gripping and cutting tasks.</data>
