    <node id="Sink">
      <data key="d0">Sink</data>
      <data key="d1">receptacle</data>
      <data key="d2">"A basin for washing."&lt;SEP&gt;The sink is a basin designed for holding water, primarily used for washing dishes or hands. It is commonly installed in kitchens and bathrooms and is often integrated into the countertop. This functionality makes it an essential fixture for hygiene and cleanliness in both domestic and commercial settings.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"hold water;"wash_dishes;"washing;"washing dishes;"washing_dishes;cleaning hands";cleaning objects";cleaning";draining";filling pots;interact for cleaning";interact with for cleaning";rinsing;store_items_temporarily"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"always located near the kitchen counter in traditional layouts"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">The sink is positioned on the right side of the workspace, recessed into the countertop. The visible portion of the sink is located near the right side of the countertop, making it a prominent feature in that area.</data>
      <data key="d7">The Sink is a kitchen fixture that serves an essential role in washing dishes and food, typically positioned near the kitchen counter. It is described as a recessed basin located on the right side of the workspace, designed to match the countertop material to create a cohesive aesthetic within the kitchen. The Sink is constructed from durable materials such as stainless steel or porcelain, which are common choices for kitchen fixtures. It effectively holds water for cleaning and washing tasks, making it a vital component of both kitchens and workspaces. Additionally, it was noted that the sink is sometimes mistakenly referenced as the location for a spatula, which is actually situated on the left counter. Overall, the Sink is an appliance designed for holding water, facilitating various tasks related to cleaning and drainage.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sink is a physical basin typically used for washing items, located on the counter in kitchens.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-6b6b9ba843c2fede51e4e70a52abeeaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-614a3c230561eadf10b09794a56e621d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efd3fa72187571ca78c00b47e8f02c04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8af5c3b71e3e01328ef854c0f92d2b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1d3449bf2ad39f130ad4bffb29c9b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd6366bae3946c6ac207bc3e435931da</data>
