    <node id="Table">
      <data key="d0">Table</data>
      <data key="d1">furniture</data>
      <data key="d2">"A rectangular brown table that can hold various objects and serve as a display surface or for meals."&lt;SEP&gt;The table is a piece of furniture characterized by a flat surface supported by one or more legs. Typically used for working or placing objects, it serves as a base for various activities. This particular table is described as having a dark blue color, adding to its aesthetic appeal. Its versatile design accommodates a range of uses, making it an essential piece of furniture in various settings.</data>
      <data key="d3">"Can be placed;"Provides a stable surface for placing objects.";"hold_various_objects;"provide stability";"provides a stable base for items";"support items;"supports placement of items";collaborate";display_surface;use_for_meals";used for holding objects or serving food.";work on</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"Global position: central in the room;Local relations: supporting various objects."&lt;SEP&gt;"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The Table is a foundational piece of furniture in a workspace environment, characterized by its flat structure, stability, and distinctive color. It occupies the lower half of an image and serves as a critical support for various objects placed upon it, which are centered on the Table. This environment is specifically designed for experiments and robotics development, making the Table an essential element for organizing and displaying necessary materials for these activities. It not only plays a vital role in the physical arrangement of the scene but also supports the overall functionality of the workspace, providing a surface for experimentation with robotic elements and facilitating collaboration among individuals. The Table serves as the primary surface in the room, accommodating various objects, including an orange cup and several toys.&lt;SEP&gt;The table is situated on the left side of an image, positioned in a distinct area away from other furniture, indicating its function as a separate space for items.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-5c168f96fe66d9dc5437d8fcd9397355&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644fac6661f7899fd96d7450bf9ca912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1b290523c83a70f613e894ce6dc953b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b9127cb8869d5c709f19137c59cad00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9b13bc6081e4cc0667d993c59416508</data>
