    <node id="Spatula">
      <data key="d0">Spatula</data>
      <data key="d1">utensil</data>
      <data key="d2">"A spatula is a kitchen utensil typically flat with a long handle, used for various cooking tasks."&lt;SEP&gt;A spatula is a kitchen utensil featuring a flat, rectangular blade that is commonly used for flipping, serving, spreading, and lifting food items. It typically has a long handle and may be constructed from a variety of materials, including metal, plastic, or silicone. The blade is often broad and flexible, making it suitable for various cooking tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;"A spatula is typically made of materials like plastic, metal, or wood and has a flat, broad blade."</data>
      <data key="d3">"Flip;"flip;"flip food;"flip pancakes;"flipping;lift cookies";lifting;serve;serve food";serve";serving";spread icing;spread sauces;spread";spreading;transferring";turn</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"avoid_using_on_non_stick_surfaces";"handle_carefully;"keep_away_from_high_heat";"may_not_be_accessible;can_be_damaged_on_non-suitable_surfaces";positioning_issues"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"Currently located on the right counter, intended for placement in the receptacle on the left counter."&lt;SEP&gt;"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;"in the kitchen, on left counter"</data>
      <data key="d7">The spatula is a versatile, flat kitchen utensil known for its broad, flat blade, which is commonly used for various cooking tasks such as flipping, spreading, and serving food. At one point, it was located on the right counter, but it was mistakenly associated with the sink location. Currently, it lies in the center of the tabletop, positioned flat and closer to a red apple. The spatula serves multiple culinary functions and is frequently found in kitchens, making it an essential tool for cooking and food preparation.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-6072d39842e7346f74b3fb1b575d857c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b6b9ba843c2fede51e4e70a52abeeaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-930680ee429708b5bdbd45cefca76bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-974e22ca070bca2dda14de3211dd57a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-120ee4f69224949414169693c31484ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ea7f411d585e076b9d1a6c98ffab476</data>
