    <node id="Indoor Environment">
      <data key="d0">Indoor Environment</data>
      <data key="d1">N/A</data>
      <data key="d2">The Indoor Environment refers to the interior space of a building, characterized by a multi-purpose living area that includes various household and functional elements. It encompasses a variety of objects and materials, featuring distinct furniture and decor elements that contribute to its overall aesthetic and functionality. This space is designed to support a range of activities and comfort, making it a versatile area within a building.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"provides_spaces_for_living;"seating;automated tasks";interacting";storage;working</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The Indoor Environment is characterized by a variety of objects and materials specifically designed to support both living and working activities. This environment is marked by its warm and inviting atmosphere, featuring elements such as wooden flooring and shelves that create a sense of comfort. Key components include a light brown wooden table, a beige area rug, a brown cabinet, and a blue robotic arm, all arranged thoughtfully to suggest either a softly lit kitchen or office space. Additionally, the space includes a sideboard, stairs, and some decorative items, contributing to its overall aesthetic and functional appeal.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-e885870d72c89234a5cac5ca26afc1be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f172317a5843d2e8c63b1d12a3baf26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a745bba3d72a571b8996b0d30c3665d7</data>
