    <node id="Right Counter">
      <data key="d0">Right Counter</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Right Counter is a rectangular wooden furniture piece situated on the right side of the kitchen. It is polished and includes cabinet doors and handles, designed to serve various purposes within the cooking space. This counter acts as a designated workspace, typically located near the sink, and is integral for tasks such as cooking, food preparation, and other kitchen activities. The surface area of the Right Counter may often appear cluttered, reflecting its functional role in the kitchen environment. Additionally, it has been noted as the specific location where a spatula was initially placed, further underscoring its utility in daily kitchen tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">"Can be utilized to store;"Can hold items;"Can hold objects;"N/A";"items can be placed;display;manipulate objects";provides storage.";serves as a surface for activities.";serves as a work surface;used for food preparation"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"None specified.";"Stability requires items to be placed centrally;"The presence of specific items (e.g., tools) can obstruct or complicate object recognition and retrieval.";overloading may lead to tipping or damage."</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">The Right Counter is positioned prominently in the lower half of the image foreground, located near the center-right of the scene beside a robotic arm. It is situated on the right side relative to another counter and was initially expected to contain LEGO items, although it ultimately held unrelated items. This counter serves a functional purpose in the workspace, specifically for moving the clamp, and it has a global position in the kitchen area, adjacent to other workspace elements.</data>
      <data key="d7">The Right Counter is a wooden surface commonly found in kitchens and laboratories, primarily utilized for placing items and engaging in various workspace activities. In the kitchen context, it serves as an essential area for organizing tools and ingredients around the sink, ensuring that everything needed for food preparation is conveniently accessible. This counter is recognized for its role as a functional workspace where diverse items, including LEGO, can be found. It is also noted for specific tasks, such as moving a clamp, showcasing its versatility in various workspace functions. Furthermore, the Right Counter is identified as the initial location of the spatula, highlighting its significance in assisting with kitchen tasks before the utensil is moved towards the left counter's receptacle. Overall, the Right Counter plays a crucial role in the organization and functionality of the kitchen workspace.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-6072d39842e7346f74b3fb1b575d857c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23be772a58e9576e74877efc6f4379dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d72875c7f15f9a08e03bb13f0f5fdb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38894c7d6a32f3a52f4c9b5cce45070b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1d3449bf2ad39f130ad4bffb29c9b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ea7f411d585e076b9d1a6c98ffab476&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce22e3f57d781d2bd14b02fff245c4be</data>
