    <node id="Clamp">
      <data key="d0">Clamp</data>
      <data key="d1">tool</data>
      <data key="d2">"A fastening device used to hold objects tightly together."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mechanical device used for holding or securing items in place."</data>
      <data key="d3">"can be picked up and moved";"tighten;adjust";loosen</data>
      <data key="d4">"requires an understood destination where items can be placed;"should_be_used_on_compatible_materials;avoid_over-tightening";ensuring the receptacle should not be a drawer if it's not appropriate"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;"initially located on the right counter."</data>
      <data key="d6">"Global position on the right counter in the kitchen; intended to be moved to the right receptacle of the left counter."&lt;SEP&gt;"right receptacle of the left counter"</data>
      <data key="d7">The Clamp is positioned on the right counter of the kitchen and is meant to be moved to the left counter's receptacle, serving a mechanical function to secure items.&lt;SEP&gt;The clamp is a tool designed to apply pressure and secure different objects together. It is important to place it in the specified receptacle to maintain organization and usability.</data>
