    <edge source="Robotic Arm" target="Spatula">
      <data key="d11">31.0</data>
      <data key="d12">The robotic arm is an automated device designed to perform various tasks, particularly in the context of cooking. It is capable of manipulating the spatula, which is a kitchen tool used for flipping, spreading, or serving food. The interaction between the robotic arm and the spatula occurs when the robotic arm picks up the spatula from a tabletop position, allowing it to perform functions that assist in automated cooking tasks. This includes moving the spatula between designated counters, thereby streamlining the cooking process and enhancing efficiency in the kitchen.</data>
      <data key="d13">automation,kitchen automation,kitchen efficiency,kitchen tasks,potential interaction,task execution,tool automation</data>
